From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 18:25:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: qualcomm: quiesce EIP VPs before zombie release

A quarantined PPE row is retained when hardware deletion fails. Clearing
VALID is best effort too, so a second command failure can leave the row
forwarding to an EIP virtual port until device teardown.

The teardown path currently drops the provider object, EIP flow and TR
before shutting down EIP VPs. Reverse that order for zombies. Clearing the
VP callback and queue mapping, followed by synchronize_net(), removes the
remaining software path before the provider releases its EIP flow and
transform references. The exported API is already shutting down, so later
provider-side VP puts are intentionally no-ops.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-ppe/-/tree/87bb9b326dfe7ddafb2cc8bc588e74d552a2a9b5
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
@@ -4333,18 +4333,19 @@ void ppe_flowtable_destroy(struct ppe_de
 	ppp_unregister_channel_notifier(&ft->ppp_nb);
 	ppe_ft_flow_drain(ft);
 
-	/* Quarantined rows were disabled when deletion failed, but deliberately
-	 * retained their provider objects while the PPE could still reference
-	 * them. Device teardown is the final point at which those EIP resources
-	 * can be released.
+	/* A quarantined row may still be valid when both delete and disable
+	 * failed. Stop EIP callbacks and queue mappings before releasing a
+	 * provider object whose flow or TR that row could still reach.
 	 */
-	list_for_each_entry(flow, &ft->zombies, zombie_node)
-		ppe_ft_eip_provider_put(flow);
+	ppe_flowtable_eip_stop(ppe_dev);
 
-	/* Provider callbacks and their full-inline flows are gone before the
-	 * exported EIP API drains outer flows and tears down EIP virtual ports.
+	/* EIP VP shutdown clears callbacks and waits for old NAPI readers. The
+	 * provider can now remove its inner EIP flow and release the TR even when
+	 * the original PPE row could not be invalidated. qcom_ppe_eip_vp_free()
+	 * is intentionally a no-op after the exported API has stopped.
 	 */
-	ppe_flowtable_eip_stop(ppe_dev);
+	list_for_each_entry(flow, &ft->zombies, zombie_node)
+		ppe_ft_eip_provider_put(flow);
 	mutex_lock(&ft->lock);
 	for (i = 0; i < PPE_FT_PPPOE_SESSIONS; i++) {
 		if (!ft->pppoe[i].ref.refcnt)
-- 
